20. Correctness argument
              For L6-level preparation, be comfortable proving why the algorithm is correct.              
              Claim              
                      The algorithm returns true iff the word exists as a valid path.
              
                    Why no valid path is missed
              
                From each current cell, we recursively examine all four legal directions.              
               Therefore, every possible adjacent path is explored unless it violates a rule:
              
                          outside grid,
                          wrong character,
                          reused cell.
              
              Those are exactly the invalid transitions.

