24. Where DP might enter later
          
          Word Search is primarily a backtracking/DFS problem.          
          But there is a deeper question:  Can memoization help?
          
          Potentially, if the state can repeat.          
          A naive state might appear to be:  (row, col, index, visitedSet)
          
          The problem is that the visited set is part of the state, and there can be many possible visited configurations.
          
          For a general grid, memoizing only: (row, col, index)          
                      is not automatically correct, because reaching the same cell/index with different 
                      previously visited cells can produce different future possibilities.
          
          This is a very important DP lesson:          
                        Before memoizing a recursive state, you must prove that the proposed state 
                        contains all information needed to determine future behavior.
          
          That's exactly the kind of mistake we want to avoid when we transition from backtracking into backtracking + memoization.


